{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-67894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{3}-2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le -1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,1\\le x\\le 10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-67894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x),$ we must compute the left and right-sided limits separately.\n\nHowever, the left-sided limit ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)$ does not exist since $f(x)$ is not defined on the interval $x\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nConsequently, the overall limit does not exist either:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-67894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41a94a11624f8b215ba481fe3c380b96753368b767f3e807082de85c9003cdc6"} {"question" "q-67894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-67894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=-2"] ["math" "{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=0"] ["math" "{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=1"] ["math" "{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=2"] ["math" "{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-67894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=\\text{DNE}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-302096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the left-sided and the right-sided limits at $x=2$ for the function\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-2 & \\text{ for }\\,x<2 \\\\ \\frac{3-\\sqrt{x+7}}{{x}^{2}-1} & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}g(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$ and $\\,$\n${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}g(x)=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-302096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Approaching from the left, we have $x<2,$ so we use the expression $g(x)={x}^{2}+x-2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}({x}^{2}+x-2) \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+2-2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x\\ge 2,$ so we use the expression $g(x)=\\frac{3-\\sqrt{x+7}}{{x}^{2}-1}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}\\frac{3-\\sqrt{x+7}}{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{2+7}}{{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{9}}{4-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-3}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{3} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}g(x)=4,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}g(x)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-302096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41a94a11624f8b215ba481fe3c380b96753368b767f3e807082de85c9003cdc6"} {"question" "q-302096" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-302096" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-302096" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-302096" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the left-sided limit at $x=\\pi $ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+\\pi  & \\text{ for }\\,x<\\pi  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge \\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{-}}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Approaching from the left, we have $x<\\pi ,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=x+\\pi .$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{-}}(x+\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\pi +\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41a94a11624f8b215ba481fe3c380b96753368b767f3e807082de85c9003cdc6"} {"question" "q-339885" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339885" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{3}+7 & \\text{ for }\\,x<-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{x-4}-1 & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$ and $\\,$\n${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}f(x)=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Approaching $x=-2$ from the left, we have $x<-2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=(x+2)^{3}+7.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}[(x+2)^{3}+7] \\\\  & =(-2+2)^{3}+7 \\\\  & ={0}^{3}+7 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, approaching $x=4$ from the right, we have $x\\ge 4,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt{x-4}-1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}(\\sqrt{x-4}-1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4-4}-1 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0}-1 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41a94a11624f8b215ba481fe3c380b96753368b767f3e807082de85c9003cdc6"} {"question" "q-339938" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339938" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339938" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-339938" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-340291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}c\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x=2 \\\\ {x}^{3}-3\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ exists. What is the value of constant $c?$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-340291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order for ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ to exist, the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal.\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $x<2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=c.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}c \\\\  & =c\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Approaching from the right, we have $x>2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={x}^{3}-3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}{x}^{3}-3 \\\\  & ={(2)}^{3}-3 \\\\  & =8-3 \\\\  & =5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the left and right-sided limits must be equal, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) \\\\ c & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-340291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41a94a11624f8b215ba481fe3c380b96753368b767f3e807082de85c9003cdc6"} {"question" "q-340291" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"} {"question" "q-340291" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014179/state.json" "file_sha256" "abe64df51b714aedce9c1a78f167446c87985dd676f7e16acb0246034be107ba"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1183 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
